    "title": "HIGHLIGHTS: Graycen Rasmussen's late goal propels Rambelles to fifth straight shutout win - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Griff McClellan ,\n47 minutes ago\nSAN ANGELO, Texas ( Concho Valley Homepage ) — The Rambelles have caught fire lately, seeking their fifth straight win.\nThe Angelo State Rambelles have put the Lone Star Conference on watch over the last several weeks, carrying a four-game win streak into their Wednesday night matchup versus the UT Tyler Patriots. The Rambelles had also outscored opponents by a margin of 8-0 over those four games. On Wednesday, the Rambelles looked to extend the streak and close their three-game homestand on a high note.\nIn four of its previous six matches, Angelo State scored a goal within the first 15 minutes of regulation. That wasn’t the case versus UT Tyler, as the teams were deadlocked in a scoreless tie at halftime.\nIn the second half, things got chippy between the two teams. Between the 70th and 87th minutes, the teams combined for four yellow cards, all of which were declared unsporting penalties. The most notable of these penalties occurred in the 70th minute, when UT Tyler’s Quinn Wolfe shoved Angelo State’s Jaycee Garza to the ground. On the very next play, the Rambelles broke the tie. Graycen Rasmussen found the top right corner of the net for her second goal of the season, giving her team the lead for good. Angelo State held on for the 1-0 win, marking its fifth straight shutout win.\nUp next: Angelo State heads north to Wichita Falls to face the Midwestern State Mustangs on Saturday, Oct 18.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to ConchoValleyHomepage.com.",
